35,2,1,talk,Mio,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Mio**: The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, like hall hire. But a third of renewals needed chasing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,- **Jonathan**: That hesitation is real. The quieter members feel uneasy about the cost per visit.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,- **Toshio**: The hours confirm it. Chasing individual payments took six hours a month. A yearly collection took barely one.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,- **Kenji**: Nine tasters refused a whole year upfront. Eleven mid-year joiners needed hand-worked calculations.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Toshio, that six-hour figure is terrifying. @Kenji, if people refuse a whole year upfront, how do we collect without that burden?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Mio, the winter social notes show they fear the math. @Takumi, does the turnout data confirm this fear is driving them away?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Jonathan, the sign-in sheets show a quarter of us do two-thirds of the work. Eighteen people never show up.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, that imbalance is real, but the hours prove the collection method is the bottleneck. We need a structure that minimizes chasing.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, the taster forms say they won’t commit to a whole year at once. @Toshio, that’s why the mid-year joiners needed hand-worked calculations.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Toshio, if yearly collection is so much lighter, why did we ever move away from it? @Kenji, can we make that easier for newcomers?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Mio, the hesitation isn't just about money; it's about feeling unwelcome. @Takumi, does the turnout drop prove that?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, the turnout drop proves people stopped feeling it was theirs. But the rota shows the same nine doing everything. We need to fix the work, not just the fee.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, we didn’t move away; we drifted. The log proves yearly collection is the only sustainable path. We must stop chasing individual payments.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, the forms say they fear the commitment, not the math. @Toshio, if we make the entry point smaller, we might keep the yearly collection simple.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, I hear you. But @Kenji, if we keep the yearly fee, how do we stop those tasters from walking away? We need a bridge.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, the bridge is clarity. If they know exactly what they are paying for, the fear of the unknown disappears.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, a bridge won’t fix the fact that eighteen people pay for nothing. We need to address the free-riders before we worry about the newcomers.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the free-riders are a symptom of the current chaos. A simple, predictable yearly fee removes the friction that lets people drift.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I hear you, but @Toshio is right. If we make the entry point smaller, we keep the yearly collection simple.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
