60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: So, what are the actual options we are choosing between? I need to see the full list before I can decide.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,- **Jonathan**: I am listening. Please share the options so we can weigh them against the hesitation I observed.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,- **Takumi**: Lay them out. I need to see if any option actually forces those eighteen ghosts to pay up or leave.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,- **Toshio**: I am ready. I need to see which option eliminates the monthly chasing burden I found in the logs.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,- **Kenji**: I’m ready too. I need to see which option lets newcomers drift in without the scary whole-year commitment.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Jonathan, I see the options now. Option A is a flat annual fee. It sounds simple, but does it solve the newcomer hesitation?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Mio, it solves the collection burden, but it ignores the fear of a whole-year commitment. It might push the tasters away.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Mio, a flat fee means those eighteen ghosts pay the same as the nine who do everything. That is exactly the unfairness I am fighting.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"-Toshio: @Takumi, the ghosts are a symptom of the current chaos. A simple, predictable yearly fee removes the friction that lets people drift.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, Option B lets them choose a smaller level. That might ease the fear of a whole year, but it adds complexity to the books.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Kenji, complexity is exactly what scares people off. @Toshio, does Option C’s small base fee make the yearly collection easier for you?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Mio, Option C is dangerous. The summer outings proved that charging per event makes people feel like guests, not members.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Jonathan, I agree. But @Mio, if the base fee is low, the ghosts still pay nothing for the work. It doesn't fix the imbalance.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"-Toshio: @Mio, Option C is the worst. It returns us to the six-hour monthly chasing nightmare. I cannot support it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Toshio, I agree. But @Mio, if we pick A, we lose the bridge for newcomers. We need a way to keep it simple but welcoming.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Kenji, I hear you. But @Toshio, the data is clear: chasing is unsustainable. I’m leaning toward A, but I need your final say.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Mio, I agree. The hesitation is about commitment, not cost. A flat fee is the only way to keep the door open without the friction.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Mio, I hate it, but the data proves C is a trap. I’ll accept A, but we must fix the rota separately.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, I support A. It is the only option that respects the hours I logged. Let us vote.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, I support A. It keeps the books simple and the door open. Let’s vote.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
